 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction and marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A guard ring is built into the junction to protect against overvoltage. The molded body uses a UL 94V-0 rated, RoHS-compliant, halogen-free compound. The terminals are solder plated and pass MIL-STD-750 method 2026 solderability. A band on the body marks the cathode, and the top carries the marking code from the part-number list."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Moisture and reflow",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 under J-STD-020, with a 260 °C peak for lead-free reflow."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 3.0 A average rating is set against lead temperature. For DSK32 to DSK36 it holds up to a lead temperature of about 91 °C and falls in a straight line to zero at 125 °C; for the higher-voltage grades it holds to about 116 °C and reaches zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "80 A is the limit for one 8.3 ms half sine. With repeated cycles the allowed peak drops, to about 34 A at 10 cycles and about 18 A at 100 cycles."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage against temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Reverse leakage rises steeply with junction temperature: at full rated reverse voltage a DSK32 to DSK34 part leaks typically about 7 µA at 25 °C, about 0.9 mA at 75 °C and about 6 mA at 100 °C. The DSK36 to DSK320 group leaks less at each temperature."
  }
 ],
